  "provider_query": "PEP 703 page that proposes making the CPython GIL optional",
  "answer": "**Official page:** [PEP 703 – Making the Global Interpreter Lock Optional in CPython](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)\n\nIt proposes a CPython build option (`--disable-gil`) so the interpreter can run without the GIL, with thread-safety changes. Author Sam Gross; sponsor Łukasz Langa; created 9 Jan 2023; targeting Python 3.13. Status is now **Final** (historical); current docs are under free-threading support. [[1]](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)\n\nRelated results:\n\n1. **[peps.python.org/pep-0703](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)** — Canonical PEP. Abstract: GIL blocks concurrent Python execution; `--disable-gil` builds define `Py_GIL_DISABLED` and use ABI tag `t`. [[2]](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/?featured_on=talkpython)\n\n2. **[Steering Council acceptance (24 Oct 2023)](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython-acceptance/37075)** — Accepted with a gradual three-phase rollout and a rollback option; “free-threaded” is the preferred term. [[3]](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython-acceptance/37075)\n\n3. **[Intent to accept (28 Jul 2023)](https://discuss.python.org/t/a-steering-council-notice-about-pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython/30474)** — Experimental in the short term (about 3.13), supported but not default later, default only long-term. [[4]](https://discuss.python.org/t/a-steering-council-notice-about-pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython/30474)\n\n4. **[PEP 779 – Criteria for supported status for free-threaded Python](https://peps.python.org/pep-0779/)** — Phase II criteria; free-threaded build officially supported in 3.14, still not the default. [[5]](https://peps.python.org/pep-0779/)\n\n5. **[GitHub PR #2955](https://github.com/python/peps/pull/2955)** — Original PEP submission by colesbury, merged 10 Jan 2023. [[6]](https://github.com/python/peps/pull/2955)\n\n6. **[Discourse: PEP discussion](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional/22606)** — Early feedback, including preferring `--disable-gil` over `--without-gil`. [[7]](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional/22606)\n\n7. **[What is PEP 703? (pydevtools)](https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-703.md)** — Summary: separate free-threaded artifact, not ABI-compatible; experimental in 3.13, supported in 3.14; default build still has the GIL. [[8]](https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-703.md)\n\n8. **[PEP 805 – Safe Parallel Python](https://peps.python.org/pep-0805/)** — Follow-on draft that builds on PEP 703 and aims for safer sharing between parallel threads. [[9]](https://peps.python.org/pep-0805/)",
